today's video has been made possible by  hellofresh stick around until the end to  find out more  with the second season of the witcher  just around the corner what better  excuse to take a look at the folklore  that inspired the franchise some of you  may have already picked up on the  creatures seen across the several  trailers as well as some of the other  more subtle hints as to what may be in  store today i'll be going over these  creatures giving you the basic witcher  lore without any spoilers but also  exploring the folklore behind them  one creature i was definitely excited to  see was the lesson or the leshi  in the books the leshi as they are known  in polish folklore are described as  forest spirits protectors of the  woodland  their ability to shapeshift makes them  very dangerous for anyone who  unknowingly wanders into their forest  in the game the leshen are known as  creatures that exist to kill  they can summon the surrounding wildlife  such as bears and wolves to aid them  their appearance is almost a cross  between an ant and the modern depiction  of a wendigo in the trailer for the show  we see the same terrifying figure but  with some minor changes the skull that  resembles a wendigo from the game is  gone it's a decision that some may not  agree with but in all honesty it's  probably closer in design to the  original stories and the folklore than  the game  the legend and stories of the leshi  across these slavic countries are fairly  similar the name itself roughly  translates to mean he from the forest  the leshi were spirits of the forest  that had a close association to hunting  which makes sense given that's where  much of it takes place  a leshi can alter its size at will from  enormous to tiny it can also alter its  likeness which is quite a valuable skill  for what is predominantly a trickster  spirit they have been known to kidnap  children who stumble into their woods as  well as leading travellers astray  despite this the leshi are not  necessarily considered evil spirits  their disposition towards humans is  mostly neutral it depends on the type of  person the leshi perceives you to be  if you treat the forest with respect you  will most likely be left alone however  those with bad intentions who show  disrespect to the forest may never find  their way home  there are also stories of parents  abandoning children in the forest who  they believe are cursed the leshi would  take these children in and raise them in  the forest as their own  as to what type of leshi we can expect  to see in the show personally i hope  they lean more towards the neutral  forest protector  in the trailer we have a scene with  geralt in a courtyard confrontation with  a dark-haired woman dressed in white the  woman lets out a piercing scream forcing  geralt to use quen to form a protective  barrier at first glance this appears to  be a banshee scream but later on in the  same courtyard we also see geralt  attacked by a giant bat with those two  things coupled together we can safely  assume this woman is a bruxer a type of  vampire the bruxer is a staple of the  games appearing in all of them in some  form  normally they appear as a woman with  long dark hair but they can also  shapeshift into large black bats  as we saw in the trailer their screams  are extremely powerful being able to  throw people across a room and even  pierce a witch's sign if the bruxer is  strong enough  they can manipulate a human's dreams  twisting and distorting them until they  become a nightmare they are also one of  the types of vampires in the witcher  that do not have an aversion to sunlight  interestingly enough out of all of the  various forms of vampires in the witcher  the bruxer is not rooted in slavic  folklore their stories can be found in  spain portugal and mexico and they are  sometimes referred to as brucia  the reason they are predominantly female  is because in their mortal lives they  were accused of being a witch having no  issues with sunlight they were  notoriously difficult to locate and kill  however they still prefer to roam at  night as that is when they are at their  most powerful it's rumored their powers  were given to them by satan himself  they fed mostly on the blood of men  children and small animals and much like  in the witcher they were able to  shapeshift into a variety of animals the  most common being a large bird a useful  form for scouring the lands undetected  once they found their victim they would  transform back into their female form  there are some differences between the  folklore and the witcher however the  influences are there to see  i assume what we will see in the show is  a vampire with some witch-like traits  and powers  in terms of talking points and  discussions for fans to have and  speculate over by far the best part of  this trailer is the scene in the forest  with what appears to be a witch's hut  the lights in the hut pan across the  screen like a spotlight that can see you  now this may just be an easter egg or a  teaser of something that may happen in a  following season but it does feel as if  they are teasing that we may see or at  least learn about the three crones  those who have played the witcher 3 will  be more than familiar with these three  figures as they provide some of the  creepiest and most unsettling scenes in  the game  the crones are three witches that live  in a cabin on the edge of the swamp they  are grotesque and haggard  however they can appear as young and  beautiful which they do to trick their  unsuspecting victims if you are lost in  their woods and stumble into their hut  they appear as three friendly helpful  sisters accept their hospitality and you  will end up being boiled and eaten  the child eating crohn's are heavily  inspired by the slavic legend of baba  yaga an old crone who lives in a hut  standing on chicken legs that can just  up and move at any time  baba yaga in slavic folklore is fairly  polarizing in some stories she is wicked  and not someone you want to cross pass  with  much of the time however she assumes the  role of the wise crone who is more than  willing to help adventurers who are  brave enough to seek her out  the witch's interpretation comes from  the idea that she also represents a  triple goddess the virgin the mother and  the crone the past present and future in  some tales she lives in a hut with her  two sisters also named baba yaga  the crones are a cd project red creation  they do not appear in the books so if we  do see them i'm sure their depiction  will be similar to the game  i think it's fair to assume that if we  do see them they will not be the main  antagonists of the season but i am sure  they will be up to no good  the witcher and slavic folklore in  general have a host of interesting and  terrifying monsters to draw from so  hopefully there will be a bunch we  haven't seen in any of the trailers i  did mean to make a video similar to this  for season 1 but never really got round  to it so here's a summary of some of the  creatures we saw in the first season  the kikimora is an insect monster that  lives underground and in swamps in the  books they are described as having a  spidery shape with large fangs in my  opinion the show does an okay job of  this design as in the games they are not  much more than just generic giant bugs  however in the show it has an almost  human head which is very creepy but it  may also draw some inspiration from the  original legend itself  in slavic folklore there are numerous  house spirits the domovoy is seen in a  positive light as it protects those who  inhabit the house  the kikimora is a female spirit that is  seen in a negative light essentially the  opposite of the domovoy it's thought  that she was the cause of sleep  paralysis by laying on your chest and  trying to strangle you similar to the  mara or nightmare of scandinavian  folklore there are also kikimora who  inhabit the swamps and bogs but they  don't have the same spider-like  appearance as they do in the witcher  they are small elderly women with  hunchbacks and pointed noses who use  moss and grass as clothing they hide by  roadsides and riverbeds kidnapping  children and knocking passersby into the  water and drowning them not exactly the  most friendly babushkas  in episode 3 we saw the appearance of a  striga a woman who has been transformed  into a monster by a curse  she is unable to control her emotions  filled with anger and hatred they lash  out and devour any living beings in  their path  the strigas do share some elements with  the romanian vampires known as the  strigoi however they are based on the  polish legend of the striga a female  demon similar to a vampire that needs to  feed on human flesh  a female demon similar to a vampire that  needs to feed on human flesh it's  believed they are born with two hearts  and two souls they even had two sets of  teeth the superstitions even went as far  to say that babies who were born with a  slightly developed teeth must have been  strigger  if the striga were killed one soul would  pass on and the remaining soul would  bring them back to life meaning they  would have to be put down twice  some other creatures we saw worthy of a  mention include the doppler the nekkers  the sylvan and the gin  hopefully we see more creatures in  season two as i really do enjoy the  witcher and slavic folklore in general  let me know which of these creatures or  characters you're most excited to see  as we mentioned earlier today's video  has been sponsored by hallo fresh  buying your own ingredients and  preparing your own meals is great but  for many with a busy schedule it's hard  to do with hellofresh you can have a  meal kit that includes fresh ingredients  and cooking instructions sent directly  to your door simply follow the  instructions provided and you have  access to all sorts of tasty meals  within half an hour each week there is a  selection of new recipes to choose from  with low carb low-fat and vegetarian  options the mill kits are sent in almost  entirely recyclable packaging so you can  even reduce your carbon footprint  i've been trying hello fresh for a few  months now and i've been extremely happy  with what i've received and the amount  of time i've been able to save some of  my favorite meals were the teriyaki  chicken and rice the honey roasted duck  with mashed potatoes and for anyone who  loves pasta dishes there are dozens to  choose from  the meals look and taste great you also  don't have to be a master chef to make  them  if you would like to try hello fresh for  yourself then go to hellofresh.com  and use code mythology 14 for up to 14  free meals and 3 free gifts  so give it a try and let me know which  meals are your favorite  as always i've been your host mythology  and fiction explained  [Music]  you

